    "amount" : null,
    "unit" : null,
    "note" : null
  } ],
  "steps" : [ "FOR THE CHICKEN AND BRINE: Combine salt, garlic, and rosemary in a bag; seal and pound until garlic cloves are crushed. Transfer to a container with 2 cups hot tap water; let stand 10 minutes. Add 1 1/2 quarts cold tap water and stir until salt dissolves. Submerge chicken in brine and refrigerate for 1 hour.", "Remove chicken from brine and pat dry. Adjust oven rack to lower-middle position and preheat oven to 450°F. Set V-rack in a small roasting pan and spray with nonstick spray.", "FOR THE PASTE: Mix rosemary, garlic, salt, 1/4 teaspoon pepper, and 1 tablespoon oil. Rub about 1 1/2 teaspoons of paste in chicken cavity. Loosen skin and slip half of paste under skin on each breast side. Tie drumsticks and tuck wings. Rub chicken with 2 teaspoons oil and season with pepper.", "FOR THE JUS: While chicken is roasting, toss garlic cloves with 1/2 teaspoon oil; add to pan after 15 minutes. Continue roasting for another 15 minutes.", "Reduce oven temperature to 375°F. Flip chicken breast-side up and brush with 1 teaspoon oil. Add broth and water to pan and roast until golden brown and thermometer reads 160°F (breast) and 175°F (thigh), adding more water as necessary. Tilt V-rack to release juices into pan and transfer chicken to a plate.", "Remove garlic cloves; scrape browned bits in pan and pour liquid into a measuring cup. Let settle; peel and mash garlic. Skim fat, should have 2/3 cup liquid (add water if needed). Transfer to saucepan with wine, rosemary, remaining broth, and garlic paste. Simmer until reduced to 1 cup. Add chicken juices, discard rosemary, adjust seasoning, and serve with chicken." ],
